{"step_index":1079,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T19:24:41Z","content":"Here is why that happened:\n\n---\n\n### The Reason: Startup Auto-Discovery of Local Files\n\nOn startup, the platform runs an **auto-loader** in `app.py`:\n\n1. It checks your local machine for existing simulation files at:\n   - `D:\\acceleration\\Model_1.csv`\n   - `D:\\acceleration\\Model_2.csv`\n   - `D:\\acceleration\\Model_3.csv`\n2. Because these 3 files **already exist on your `D:\\` drive**, the platform automatically parsed and analyzed them on startup so you don't have to manually upload a 50,000-row file every time the page refreshes during a live judge demo.\n3. Therefore, **it WAS reading real data** — directly from the files on your disk.\n\n---\n\n### What Happens if There are No Files on Disk?\n\nIf those files did not exist and you hadn't uploaded anything:\n- `st.session_state.model_data` would be empty (`{}`).\n- The system would display an empty state banner:\n  > *\"Upload inspection images and production datasets to generate causal links.\"*\n- **No root causes or bottleneck cards would appear** until you uploaded a file.\n\n---\n\n### What Happens if You Upload a New / Different File in the Sidebar?\n\nWhen you upload a new file via the sidebar (or enter a custom path):\n1. The system **immediately overrides** the auto-loaded dataset with your newly uploaded file.\n2. It recalculates the station metrics, identifies the new bottleneck, and updates the root-cause cards in real time.","thinking":"The code snippet hints at an auto-loading mechanism for default model files. This behavior could be the source of the pre-existing root cause. If the application attempts to load a default model at startup, it could trigger the observed issue even without explicit user upload.\n\n\n"}
