{"step_index":1103,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T19:32:13Z","content":"**`3000Samplesv3.mat`** is the **MATLAB Training Dataset Workspace** containing 3,000 simulation data points exported from Rockwell Arena to train the Artificial Neural Network (ANN) surrogate models.\n\n---\n\n### What is Inside `3000Samplesv3.mat`:\n\nThe binary `.mat` workspace contains the predictor inputs and response outputs for all three simulation models:\n\n1. **Model 1 Data**:\n   - `Model1Predictors` & `Model1Response` (Inputs and outputs used to train `Model1ANN.m`).\n2. **Model 2 Data**:\n   - `Model2PredictorDrilling`, `Model2ResponseDrilling`\n   - `Model2PredictorMilling`, `Model2ResponseMilling`\n   - `Model2PredictorAssembly`, `Model2ResponseAssembly`\n   (Used to train `Model2ANN.m`).\n3. **Model 3 Multi-Station Data**:\n   - `Model3Predictors`\n   - `Model3Answerc1s2` (Cell 1 Station 2)\n   - `Model3Answerc1s4` (Cell 1 Station 4)\n   - `Model3Answerc2s2`, `Model3Answerc2s4`\n   - `Model3Answerc3s2`, `Model3Answerc3s3`\n   - `Model3Answerc4s3`, `Model3Answerc4s4`\n   (Used to train all 8 cell-station surrogate models: `c1s2ANN.m` through `c4s4ANN.m`).\n\n---\n\n### How it Connects to the Project Architecture:\n\n$$\\text{Rockwell Arena (3,000 Simulation Runs)} \\xrightarrow{\\text{Exported to}} \\mathbf{3000Samplesv3.mat} \\xrightarrow{\\text{MATLAB nftool / fitnet}} \\text{13 ANN Neural Models (.m)} \\xrightarrow{\\text{Vectorized In}} \\text{Tab 5 Digital Twin}$$\n\n1. **Arena Simulation**: 3,000 Monte Carlo runs were executed in Rockwell Arena across different machine parameters.\n2. **Data Packaging**: Arena simulation inputs and outputs were saved into `3000Samplesv3.mat`.\n3. **ANN Training**: MATLAB's Neural Network Fitting tool loaded `3000Samplesv3.mat` to train 2-layer feedforward networks (10 hidden tansig neurons).\n4. **Platform Digital Twin (Tab 5)**: Our Python engine parsed those neural network weights from the resulting `.m` files to create the real-time Digital Twin.\n\n---\n\n### How to Explain This to the Judges:\n> *\"3000Samplesv3.mat is our empirical training database containing 3,000 discrete-event simulation runs from Rockwell Arena. We used these 3,000 samples to train our 13 Neural Network surrogate models in MATLAB, which our platform now executes in under 0.05ms as a real-time digital twin.\"*","thinking":"Initial examination reveals data organized into three distinct models, each with predictors, responses, and answers. Model 2's structure is more granular, differentiating between assembly, drilling, and milling operations, implying specialized prediction components. Model 3 appears to have multiple answer categories.\n\n\n"}
